            <ArticleTitle>Postoperative analgesia after circumcision. A randomized comparison between caudal analgesia and intramuscular morphine in boys.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>552-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A randomised blind comparison between caudal analgesia (1.5 mg/kg bupivacaine) and intramuscular morphine (0.15 mg/kg) is reported. Forty boys were studied. Caudal analgesia is shown to be significantly better than morphine by means of a linear analogue scale designed to quantify behaviour immediately after operation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
